+    if: c.fputs("# node owns (lmx_walk_load_body).  OWN and OWN_OF read the row, SET and SET_OF write it and mark it dirty;\n# a slot with no row is the translator's broken promise, said as \"lmx: invariant: an own field used but\n# not loaded\" (X1).\n# The publication (lmx_walk_publish) writes the dirty rows into their slots in row order and unmarks\n# them: at CALL after its arguments, at PRIM_PUB after its operands, and when the activation ends --\n# RET after its value, a fall-off, a throw that leaves.  AT, PUT, PUT_REF, OF and PUT_OF are explicit\n# graph operations and never see the table: a write through them leaves the working value as it is.\n# Nothing is reloaded after a call, and a clean row is never written back.  Activation state lives\n# only on LmxWalkFrame and in its scratch slice; nothing precomputes or caches a field set (k.4).\n# MUL/DIV/MOD: [mul|div|mod, a, b]; typed numeric result. A zero divisor or\n# signed arithmetic overflow on a complete operation raises the ordinary\n# implicit `interpreter` throw (THROWN + LMX_WALK_NAME_INTERPRETER, no extra\n# children); malformed operands stay INVALID.\n# PUT_OF (-177 c4 / D-54): [put_of, struct-expr, slot, value]; holder evaluated.\n# D-105 (Q39): OF [of, struct-expr, slot, req] and PUT_OF [put_of, struct-expr, slot, value, req] --\n# a non-null req is the named Structure the place is typed with: the slot is an EDGE into the\n# `implements` table's correspondence (K01): below req's width it is req's own field (an explicit\n# `[N]name` use), from width to 2*width-1 the LAST half of field slot - width (a bare `name` use,\n# the value's last occurrence of it).  lmx_implements_slot resolves the edge to the value's own\n# slot; no record = INVALID.\n# A physical reference place can additionally carry the closed pointer-cell witness supplied by its declaration:\n# AT [at, slot, unused, pointer-witness], OF [of, holder, slot, optional-req, pointer-witness], and PUT_OF\n# [put_of, holder, slot, value, optional-req, pointer-witness]. The witness is checked before the live slot's kind\n# or value is read; an absent cell is not the valid null held by a present typed cell. The same canonical ABI is\n# required for the witness and slot even when both addresses came from another admitted arena.\n# lmx_walk_slot refuses an OP-node holder (X1). receiveMessage take (-177 c1): PRIM record whose fn is lmx_walk_mail_take (nargs 0);\n# Empty inbox yields a present null reference under its declared result contract.\n# lmx_walk_admit / lmx_walk_admit_letter consume two reference-value storage inputs;\n# letter admits its payload. YES preserves the reference; NO throws IMPLEMENTS.\n# lmx_walk_merge_model is the existing explicit runtime merge callback; this\n# carrier description does not define source declaration/call classification.\n# CALL/EXEC child3 and PRIM.signature share the ordinary two-part contract:\n# child0 is the ordered input-witness Structure; child1 is an empty return part\n# for void, or contains one result witness. The contract is declared metadata,\n# never inferred from supplied operands, used ARG nodes or a callable's data child0.\n#\n#   ret     [ret, value?]                 return an optional typed value\n#   call    [call, code, data, contract, catch, actuals...]\n#             code/data identify the selected complete callable occurrence;\n#             its native word selects native adapter or ordinary walk.\n#   exec    [exec, data?, target-expression, contract, catch, actuals...]\n", f) < 0
