sage's arena (to tell a Structure from a cell among the fields of a body)\n# and the execution context's temporary-frame store. Builder roles may be\n# supplied, but are not required to interpret an already-built graph.\nstruct: LmxWalkContext\n    @: LmxArena arena\n    @: LmxScratch scratch\n    @: Lmx roles\n    # Physical address of the ordinary receiver-expression graph value denoting the exact\n    # independent+const+immutable profile.  Zero means this program declares no such profile.\n    @: Lmx immutable_profile\n    # Borrow the existing qualified-root span, not a second graph or name map.\n    @@: Lmx immutable_roots\n    size_t: immutable_root_count\n    # How many times this unit has asked the arena's index what an address is.\n    size_t: classified\n    # N4 (SF14): 1 while an EXEC with explicit data enters its walked callee; that entry takes it (LmxWalkFrame.split)\n    # and clears it, so no activation nested in the callee inherits it.\n    int: split_entry\nend: LmxWalkContext\n\n# One activation.  An automatic object of lmx_walk_run; nothing of it is in the graph.\nstruct: LmxWalkFrame\n    @: LmxWalkContext context\n    @: LmxArena arena\n    @: Lmx roles\n    # The selected code, the source model of its data fields, and the actual data: `code`\n    # retains the selected occurrence and native identity; `source` is the physical\n    # Structure whose field coordinates the body uses; `node` supplies those fields.\n    # For a direct flat call all three are M. For an explicit code/data call,\n", f) < 0
