+    if: c.fputs("# Fixed LmxDec ABI: coefficient storage is 34 digits in every TU.\n#\n# The C form this replaces tested the macro before defining it --\n# \"#if defined(DECNUMDIGITS) / #if DECNUMDIGITS != 34 / #error ... / #else / #define\n# DECNUMDIGITS 34 / #endif\" -- because a different preexisting DECNUMDIGITS must be a\n# compile error, not a resize.  L1 defines the macro; decNumber.h only defines its\n# own default \"if not defined\", so with this header first 34 wins, and a TU that\n# fixed a different value first gets the compiler's redefinition diagnostic.  What\n# is NOT expressed here is a compile-time \"\"must equal 34\"\" test of an already\n# defined macro: L1 has no conditional composition over a defined name (gap\n# recorded, not worked around with raw C -- spec 1.9 forbids the hatch for this).\ndefine: DECNUMDIGITS 34\n", f) < 0
